+/*
+ * VitaBrowser patch 254: WebAssembly (see macsurf_wasm.h).
+ *
+ * QuickJS has no WebAssembly. hCaptcha's proof of work is a WebAssembly
+ * module (docs/wasm-hcaptcha-measurement.md), and wasm-bindgen / emscripten
+ * output turns up wherever a site ships Rust or C. This is the engine
+ * side: wasm3 runs the code; the natives below give JavaScript what the
+ * WebAssembly API needs.
+ *
+ *  - __wasm.parse(bytes): a module handle, with the module's imports and
+ *    exports read from its own sections (wasm3 keeps export names for
+ *    functions and globals only, not memories and tables), or the error.
+ *    wasm3 parses the structure here; function bodies compile on first
+ *    call, as wasm3 does (a whole-module compile is seconds on the Vita).
+ *  - __wasm.newMemory(pages, maximum): a WebAssembly.Memory made by a
+ *    script -- a wasm3 runtime with no module yet, so its ArrayBuffer is
+ *    wasm3's memory from the start (emscripten keeps the views it made
+ *    before instantiating).
+ *  - __wasm.instantiate(module, functions, memory): an instance -- its own
+ *    wasm3 environment, runtime and copy of the bytes (wasm3 points into
+ *    them), or, for a module importing memory, that memory's runtime,
+ *    which wasm3 then leaves as it is -- with each function import linked
+ *    to a trampoline that calls the JavaScript function; then the start
+ *    function.
+ *  - __wasm.func(instance, index): a JavaScript function for a wasm
+ *    function (an export, or a table entry).
+ *  - __wasm.memBuffer / memGrow / memPages: the memory as an ArrayBuffer
+ *    over wasm3's own bytes. wasm3 reallocates memory when it grows, so
+ *    an ArrayBuffer handed out is detached as soon as the bytes move --
+ *    checked whenever control leaves WebAssembly -- and wasm-bindgen's
+ *    "byteLength === 0" cache check then fetches the new one.
+ *  - __wasm.globalGet / globalSet, tableGet / tableLength, detach.
+ *
+ * Errors: a trap becomes "RuntimeError: ..." for the JavaScript side to
+ * throw as WebAssembly.RuntimeError; an exception thrown by an import is
+ * kept, the call unwinds with a trap, and the same exception is rethrown
+ * from the export call. Re-entrant calls (an import calling an export --
+ * wasm-bindgen does it for every string it returns) are wasm3's own: it
+ * moves the runtime's stack base to the import's frame for the duration.
+ *
+ * Time: the whole call -- slices included -- is subtracted from the
+ * script's runaway clock (macsurf_qjs_pause_script_clock); JavaScript run
+ * by imports counts as usual. A call that runs WASM_CALL_CAP_MS, or that
+ * the user stops in a slice, ends in a RuntimeError.
+ */
